##! `/self/search/open` and `/module/search/open`: a view over
##! `source` from `from`, filled by `pattern`'s matches. `open`
##! answers a `Rd`; `/self/search/<n>` and `/module/search/<n>` are
##! its shape, `n` a count from 0 that never goes back.
##!
##! `seek` is the journey a line makes. A `/` or an `M-x search`
##! opens one view at its first key and seeks it at every key
##! after, reading the same `matches` and `progress` as it goes:
##! one view and one call a key, never a view a key. A `Seek`'s
##! `view` drops the list it holds and fills again from `from`
##! with `pattern`, over the source it was opened on and the
##! length `open` measured; both cells read the new fill from the
##! next read on. A pattern that does not parse is `Invalid` and
##! the view keeps the list it had, so a half-typed line still
##! shows the last whole one; a `view` that is no view of this
##! Module's is `Invalid`.
##! search api, version 1.
## The Open type.
pub type Open {
    ## The source field.
    pub source: Rd<()>,
    ## The pattern field.
    pub pattern: String,
    ## The ignorecase field.
    pub ignorecase: Bool,
    ## The smartcase field.
    pub smartcase: Bool,
    ## The from field.
    pub from: U64,
}
## The Seek type.
pub type Seek {
    ## The view field.
    pub view: Rd<()>,
    ## The pattern field.
    pub pattern: String,
    ## The ignorecase field.
    pub ignorecase: Bool,
    ## The smartcase field.
    pub smartcase: Bool,
    ## The from field.
    pub from: U64,
}
## The Match type.
pub type Match {
    ## The over field.
    pub over: Rd<()>,
    ## The at field.
    pub at: U64,
    ## The len field.
    pub len: U64,
}
## Needs WRITE.
pub open: (h: Rd<search.search>) -> (source: Rd<()>) -> (pattern: String) -> (ignorecase: Bool) -> (smartcase: Bool) -> (from: U64) -> Rd<()>
## Needs WRITE.
pub seek: (h: Rd<search.search>) -> (view: Rd<()>) -> (pattern: String) -> (ignorecase: Bool) -> (smartcase: Bool) -> (from: U64) -> ()
